      "name": "clinical_problem_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Categorizes the nature of patient need (acute vs chronic vs preventive etc.), a genuine grouping axis directly serving 'what patient needs appear.' Values are sound readings, though the annual physical labeled chronic_management is a mild stretch (arguably preventive), and MI follow-up as chronic is well-grounded."
    },
    {
      "name": "acuity_and_threat",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a severity axis. Partially redundant with the existing 'urgency' column but offers a finer-grained clinical reading (e.g. acute_stable, life_threatening) beyond raw triage urgency, so it retains some leverage. Values align well with source text."
    },
    {
      "name": "intervention_required",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Captures what action the need calls for (pharmaceutical, imaging, procedural), a strong new axis for the query. Well grounded: doxycycline->pharmaceutical, MRI->imaging_diagnostic. Annual physical->pharmaceutical is slightly weak since labs were ordered, not clearly a drug, but broadly defensible."
    },
    {
      "name": "anatomic_system_focus",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Body-system categorization gives a clear grouping axis for patient needs. Values are well extracted from text (respiratory URI, cardiovascular MI, musculoskeletal knee, dermatologic acne)."
    },
    {
      "name": "care_coordination_requirement",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Distinct downstream axis about follow-up/referral/admission needs, useful for the query. Values are warranted inferences (MRI to rule out tear->specialist_referral; return-if-worse URI->not_present; MI regimen continuation->long_term_followup)."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.83,
  "source_groundedness": 0.86,
  "rationale": "The added columns provide multiple genuinely distinct analytical axes (problem type, acuity, intervention, anatomic system, coordination) that each help answer what patient needs appear in visit notes. acuity_and_threat overlaps somewhat with the original urgency column but still adds clinical granularity. Values across sampled rows are sound extractions or well-warranted inferences from the reason_for_visit text, with only minor stretches (annual physical labeled chronic/pharmaceutical). No fabricated facts observed."
}

